<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Engineering wins $85 mln Saudi order.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Engineering wins $85 mln Saudi order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ssangyong Engineering and Construction Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Ssangyong Group, said on Wednesday it has won an $85 million order to expand the Hadeed steel mill in Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>A company official said the expansion, due to be completed by November 1998, would raise the still mill's annual capacity to 2.3 million tonnes from the current 1.5 million.</p>
<p>The order was received from Voest-Alpine of Austria, which is responsible for all construction works on the Saudi steel mill, he said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
